{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>My thoughts</b> — my musings. And in the language of Kedar, a thing that binds, and this is the binding of thought." "<b>My heart's portions</b> — according to the context, weary ones. And the Gaon [Saadia], of blessed memory, said: it is from את מורשיהם by a distant path."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The phrase 'כפי העניין שעיפים' is textually difficult; read hyper-literally as 'according to the matter, weary ones.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:53.663198572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}